  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through Sunday)\nIssued at 858 PM CDT Sun Oct 25 2026\n\nAnother ridge will attempt to build back into the Tennessee Valley\nlate this week, resulting in sunny/dry weather Thursday and Friday\nand highs climbing to around 80 degrees each day. The ridge will\nbegin to shift east on Saturday, with an area of low pressure\ndeveloping over Texas and the lower Mississippi Valley Saturday\nnight into Sunday. As it stands right now, Saturday (Halloween)\nlooks to be a warm/dry day with increasing cloud cover -- with\npotentially some low rain chances returning to the forecast\nSaturday evening. Medium chances of showers will return to the\nforecast late Saturday night into Sunday as the low quickly shifts\neastward across the Deep South. This will give the Tennessee\nValley, it's best shot at appreciable rainfall in a couple weeks.\nWe will need to resolve the timing of the system better, but our\ngreatest confidence appears to be on Sunday for now.",
